From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 04:35:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vs995: skip the ELF check on libkeystore_binder

The blob's DT_NEEDED still names libbinder-v32.so, which 24.0 does not
build, so check_elf_file fails once the dependency is no longer declared in
shared_libs:

  libkeystore_binder.so: error: DT_NEEDED "libbinder-v32.so" is not
  specified in shared_libs.

Declaring it again is not an option -- the module does not exist on this
branch -- so the two halves go together: drop the dependency, and stop
checking a recorded dependency that cannot be satisfied. The library is
reached only through the keymaster@3.0 blob; whether that path still works
on 24.0 is a runtime question this cannot answer.
---
 Android.bp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 8cce851..a1fa22b 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -92,6 +92,7 @@ cc_prebuilt_library_shared {
 		},
 	},
 	compile_multilib: "both",
+	check_elf_files: false,
 	prefer: true,
 }
 
